**Branch:** issue-269-bug-horniness-not-rolled-without-igamecl
**Commit:** c82df2e
**Tests:** 1211 core + 443 adapter = 1654 passing, 0 failures
**Deviations from contract:** none

## Summary

- `headerOption()` was missing `.argParser(collectValues).default([])`, so Commander passed the raw string to `parseHeaders()` instead of an array
- Iterating a string with `for (const header of headers)` yields individual characters, so `"X-Test: hello"` would error on `"X"` (no colon found)
- Affects all commands using `--header`: `generate`, `generate-crd`, `generate-jsonschema`, `download`

## Root cause

```typescript
// Before (broken): Commander passes string, not string[]
return new Option('--header <header>', '...');

// After (fixed): Commander collects into array
return new Option('--header <header>', '...')
  .argParser(collectValues)
  .default([]);
```

## Test plan

- [x] Existing `parseHeaders` tests pass (41/41)
- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit` passes

Both maps in the before/after comparison were fully non-interactive (`scrollZoom`/`dragPan` disabled, `initialViewState` uncontrolled), making zoom useless — each map was an independent static snapshot with no way to navigate or align them.

## Changes

- **Shared controlled `viewState`**: Both maps now share a single `viewState` driven by `onMove`, so any zoom or pan on either side instantly mirrors to the other
- **Interaction re-enabled**: `scrollZoom` and `dragPan` are now active; they are only suppressed while the divider handle is being dragged to prevent accidental panning mid-slide
- **Deduplication**: Shared map props extracted into a `sharedMapProps` object

```js
const [viewState, setViewState] = useState({ ...ROMANIA_CENTER, zoom });

const sharedMapProps = {
  viewState,
  onMove: (evt) => setViewState(evt.viewState),
  scrollZoom: !isDragging,
  dragPan: !isDragging,
  // ...
};
```

Both maps now stay pixel-perfectly aligned on zoom/pan, so dragging the divider bar correctly reveals the 2020 vs 2024 delta at whatever location and zoom level you're inspecting.

Consumers of `getBaseConfig` had no way to pass options to the display name plugin, forcing a post-call mutation hack (find plugin tuple by string key, mutate options in-place). Adds a `displayName` parameter that is spread directly into the plugin's options.

```js
// Before — consumers had to do this:
const baseConfig = getBaseConfig(api);
const displayNamePlugin = baseConfig.plugins.find(
  (p) => p[2] === '@mui/internal-babel-plugin-display-name',
);
displayNamePlugin[1].allowedCallees ??= {};
displayNamePlugin[1].allowedCallees['@base-ui/utils/fastHooks'] = ['fastComponent', 'fastComponentRef'];

// After:
const baseConfig = getBaseConfig({
  displayName: {
    allowedCallees: {
      '@base-ui/utils/fastHooks': ['fastComponent', 'fastComponentRef'],
    },
  },
});
```

The `displayName` object is spread into the plugin options (`{ ...displayName }`), so any future display name plugin options are automatically forwarded without further changes to `getBaseConfig`.

Four independent bugs in the death-drop tracking and GUI systems, ranging from permanent data loss on chunk unload to a classic TOCTOU memory leak and a client-server inventory desync.

## Fix 1 — Chunk unload destroys tracking data permanently
`EntityLeaveLevelEvent` fires on **chunk unload**, not just despawn. The old code called `untrackOwnedDropEntity` unconditionally, removing the entity's integer ID from `OWNED_DEATH_DROP_IDS` and `ENTITY_DIMENSIONS`. When the chunk reloads, the entity gets a **new** runtime integer ID — with no `EntityJoinLevelEvent` handler, it was never re-tracked.

Added `onEntityJoinLevel`: for any `ItemEntity` that joins a server-side level, always register it in `ALL_ITEM_ENTITY_DIMENSIONS`; if it also carries `IS_DEATH_DROP=true` and a non-sentinel `OWNER_UUID` (both serialized to NBT, so they survive the chunk round-trip), re-add it to `OWNED_DEATH_DROP_IDS` and `ENTITY_DIMENSIONS` under its new integer ID. Private highlighting and void recovery now survive chunk unload/reload cycles transparently.

## Fix 2 — TOCTOU race leaks `ENTITY_DIMENSIONS` entries forever
```java
// Thread A removes last ID → tracked is now empty
tracked.remove(item.getId());
// Thread B calls computeIfAbsent, gets the empty set, adds newId, writes ENTITY_DIMENSIONS[newId]
if (tracked.isEmpty()) {
    OWNED_DEATH_DROP_IDS.remove(owner); // ← wipes Thread B's new entry too
    // ENTITY_DIMENSIONS[newId] now leaks forever
}
```
Replaced with `OWNED_DEATH_DROP_IDS.compute(owner, (ownerUuid, tracked) -> { ... })`, which holds the per-key lock for the entire remove-and-check-empty operation.

## Fix 3 — Ghost items in `SnapshotChestMenu`
Clicking any non-action slot in the upper chest returned early without syncing. The client's optimistic "cursor item placed" update was never corrected by the server, producing a permanent ghost item.

Added a `ClientboundContainerSetSlotPacket(-1, this.incrementStateId(), getCarried())` resync for all upper-chest clicks that don't dispatch an action, forcing the client to revert the phantom placement.

## Fix 4 — `EntityTickEvent.Pre` global broadcast for ALL_DROPS mode
`EntityTickEvent.Pre` fires once per entity per tick — 5 000 entities × 20 TPS = 100 000 event dispatches/sec just to early-return for non-ItemEntity types.

Introduced `ALL_ITEM_ENTITY_DIMENSIONS: Map<Integer, ResourceKey<Level>>`, maintained by the new `onEntityJoinLevel` / `onEntityLeaveLevel` handlers (cheap HashMap ops on entity join/leave). `onServerTick` now iterates this map for `ALL_DROPS` mode recovery instead. The `onEntityTick` handler and its `EntityTickEvent` import are removed entirely.

